{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/8031","id":5222577740,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABN0o2TA","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8031","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8031.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8031.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8031","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/8031/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/8031/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8031/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/4a0fda1c84571e15755a8d1b359818d75e7ad58e","number":8031,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(id): F12.9 program upgrade with state migration and rollback (#1066)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## F12.9 program upgrade with state migration and rollback (#1066)\n\nImplements the confirmed F12.9 remainder for task 12962, now that the gate has landed: issue #1065 (F12.8 guest SDKs) closed via PR #7891 (merged 2026-11-09T01:03Z), verified fresh at claim time. Before this PR, `pkgs/id/src/world/` had no upgrade module, no migrate export, no versioned program-state snapshot format, and no upgrade runner.\n\n### What lands\n\nNew module `pkgs/id/src/world/upgrade.rs`, re-exported from `crate::world`:\n\n- **Versioned snapshot format for world program state** — `ProgramSnapshot` with a magic + format-version envelope. Format v1 (magic, one version byte, raw state) is still decoded so old snapshots upgrade; everything new is encoded at the current format v2 (version, state length, state, FNV-1a checksum), and the decoded snapshot records the format version it was read from.\n- **Optional `migrate` export in the guest ABI** — the `MigrateExport` host-side contract: `migrate(state, from_version, to_version) -> Result<state>`. Programs without the export (`None`) keep working under the pre-existing behavior: their state is carried across the upgrade byte-for-byte.\n- **Probe-first upgrade runner** — `upgrade_program` decodes and migrates a probe copy of the state, re-encodes it at the current snapshot format, and reads it back; the running program's version and snapshot are swapped only if the migrated state round-trips exactly. Any failure (migrate refuses, migrated state over the 4 MiB bound, round-trip mismatch) leaves the old program bit-for-bit unchanged — that is the rollback.\n\n### Exit tests (plan, Phase 12 F12.9)\n\nIn-module tests, each naming its oracle:\n\n- `counter_upgrades_across_a_snapshot_format_change` — a v1 ASCII-decimal counter in a v1 snapshot upgrades to a v2 little-endian counter in a current-format snapshot, same value.\n- `failing_upgrade_leaves_the_old_program_running` — a deliberately failing `migrate` leaves version and snapshot bytes unchanged.\n- Plus: current-format round-trip records its version, legacy v1 snapshots still decode, corrupted snapshots are refused, no-`migrate` programs carry state unchanged, oversized migrated state rolls back.\n\nTargeted tests run on the laptop before opening (`cargo test --lib world::upgrade`: 7 passed); full verification is CI per fleet policy.\n\n### Scope notes\n\n- No F12.8 work (issue #1065, landed separately) and no F12.15 work (issue #558, the downstream consumer of this migration path).\n- The runner is the transport-independent core seam (alongside the BUILDER-gated program install/upgrade path in `world/mod.rs`); wiring it into a live hot-swap command is follow-up work, not hidden in this PR.\n\n<!-- agent-note:v1 -->\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796812941&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8031&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8031&signature=afc384298ac8166af81607869195b9455988158e0a8c483a05ae42119f99d41f\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/8031?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T10:42:17Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T13:37:52Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T